#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
"""One machine-wide queue of card submissions for all owners (decision 0033: at most five jobs of the
account in the Slurm queue, pending, held and running together, over all owners).

One route: card runs are submitted only by `nrpic-queue add`; `nrpic-run submit` with a card launcher
(batch, chain) is for the dispatcher, which marks the commands it runs (NRPIC_QUEUE_DISPATCH=<id>:<token>,
inherited by a --cmd wrapper that calls nrpic-run inside). Called directly, nrpic-run refuses and prints the
`nrpic-queue add` line to use instead; `nrpic-run submit --dry-run` stays open to everyone. Outside a
dispatch, a local run of nrpic-run and `nrpic-env exec` put harness/shims/slurm first on the command's PATH,
where sbatch, srun and salloc are stubs that refuse (exit 2) whatever form the command takes; inside a
dispatch PATH is left alone, so nothing of the stubs reaches a job. A call by absolute path (/usr/bin/sbatch)
passes: only a limit on the Slurm side or the tool-guard hook closes that. The dispatcher's cap keeper
reports an excess that came in by any way; it cancels nothing.

    harness/bin/nrpic-queue add --label L [--after LABEL] [--priority N] [--note TEXT] [--no-check]
                                -- <the arguments of `nrpic-run submit`>
    harness/bin/nrpic-queue add --label L [--after LABEL] [--priority N] [--note TEXT] --cmd 'LINE'
    harness/bin/nrpic-queue list [--all] [--owner ID]
    harness/bin/nrpic-queue show ID
    harness/bin/nrpic-queue status
    harness/bin/nrpic-queue remove ID          a waiting entry (an owner its own entries, orch any)
    harness/bin/nrpic-queue retry ID           a failed entry back to waiting (same rule; not while a job of it
                                               is queued)
    harness/bin/nrpic-queue mark-done ID       a submitted or failed entry of which no job is queued
    harness/bin/nrpic-queue check-dispatch     exit 0 only inside a valid dispatch (for --cmd wrappers)
    harness/bin/nrpic-queue run [--poll S] [--cmd-timeout S] [--keeper S] [--keeper-confirm S]   (orch)
    harness/bin/nrpic-queue stop [--wait S]                                                       (orch)
    harness/bin/nrpic-queue clear-alert                                                           (orch)

Start the dispatcher once (orchestrator, standing in the main checkout; it outlives the session):

    cd /data/haiyangw/nrpic && mkdir -p locks/queue && setsid nohup /usr/bin/python3 -I \\
      /data/haiyangw/nrpic/harness/bin/nrpic-queue run >> /data/haiyangw/nrpic/locks/queue/nohup.out 2>&1 < /dev/null &

Stop it: `cd /data/haiyangw/nrpic && harness/bin/nrpic-queue stop` (writes locks/queue/STOP; the dispatcher
ends within a second unless an entry's command is running, and removes the file; queued card jobs are left
alone). The pause flag locks/PAUSE does not stop it: a card run uses none of the account's usage (decision
0026 item 2); its presence is logged.

Who and where (identity from the path). A command that changes the queue (add, remove, retry, mark-done,
run, stop, clear-alert) acts on the worktree the caller stands in; -C must name that same worktree, except
for the orchestrator standing in the main checkout, who may name any (`-C wt/<ID> add ...` queues a run for
that owner). From a data root of the main checkout (scratch/, locks/, ...) or outside a worktree these
commands refuse. run, stop and clear-alert need the caller in the main checkout. list, show, status read
from anywhere. Any copy of this command may be called; the state belongs to the machine.

Entries. Either the arguments of an `nrpic-run submit` call after `--` (a leading `submit` or
`harness/bin/nrpic-run submit` is dropped; the launcher must be batch or chain; `nrpic-run submit
--dry-run` checks them at once unless --no-check), or with --cmd any command line that submits at most
one job, run with bash in the worktree root (a wrapper that continues a cut chain from its restart file;
it tests its dispatch with `nrpic-queue check-dispatch`, never by the marker being set: a job the wrapper
submits itself inherits the variable). --after LABEL: wait until that entry of the same owner (the last one
added with that label) is done, that is until none of its jobs is in squeue; an entry after one that failed
or was removed stays blocked until that one is retried or this one removed. --priority N: 0 first, default
5; 0 and 1 are the orchestrator's (0 for runs a user request waits for; 2 for runs a gate package waits
for); a waiting entry improves by one class per AGING_HOURS (8) hours, never past 1, so nothing starves
(`list` shows the effective priority). Labels are 1 to 48 of [A-Za-z0-9._-], unique per owner among entries
not done or removed.

States. waiting -> submitting (the dispatcher runs its command) -> submitted (the command exited 0; the
run id and Slurm job ids it printed are kept, and the job's name: nrpic-run names a job after its run id,
and a chain resubmits itself under that name) -> done (no job of that name or id in squeue at two looks
in a row). failed: the command exited non-zero for another reason than those below, timed out
(--cmd-timeout, default 900 s), or was running when the dispatcher ended; what it submitted is recorded
on every outcome, so retry and mark-done refuse while such a job is queued; `list` shows the first line of
its stderr, `show` all of it. removed: by remove. A job is the entry's by its id (printed by its command and
new at that dispatch, array tasks included), or by name only when the name is the entry's own run id (a
chain's segments); never by a generic name such as `batch`, so a job of the user's that carries the same
name does not keep the entry submitted, and two entries never claim one job.
Waits, not failures (the entry stays waiting, `list` and `show` say "waits: <reason> since <time>"): nrpic-run
refused for the queue cap ("queue cap: ...": a job came in between the two counts, e.g. a chain's next
segment); nrpic-run refused because the worktree is not clean (tried again every fifth look until it is
clean); the worktree is in the middle of a merge, rebase, cherry-pick or revert (passed over until it ends).

The dispatcher, at each look (every POLL seconds, default 120): runs the cap keeper; marks submitted
entries done; then, while the account has fewer than QUEUE_CAP jobs in squeue (harness/lib/nrpic_harness.py,
the count nrpic-run uses; `squeue -r`, so every task of a job array counts) and an entry may be dispatched,
takes the next one: the lowest effective priority; within it, the owner served longest ago (round robin);
within the owner, the order of adding. It holds the machine's submit lock (locks/queue/submit.lock) from
the count immediately before the submission, through the entry's command, to the count after it. The
command's output goes to files (out/<id>.<n>.stdout, .stderr, then .log), never pipes, so that a child it
leaves behind cannot hold the dispatcher; its process group is recorded in the entry, what is left of it
when the command ends is ended, and a restart ends the group of a command the previous dispatcher left
running before its first look. If the account's jobs rose by more than one around a dispatch (every job
new at that dispatch counts, a job the user submits by hand in those seconds too; a job the command printed
always counts; one unprinted job per name of a running job is a chain's next segment) that is a violation
of the one route: it stops submitting, logs ALERT and writes locks/queue/ALERT until the orchestrator runs
clear-alert. It never finishes runs: the owner closes them (`nrpic-run finish <run_id>`) as before.

The cap keeper reports, it never cancels: every KEEPER (30) seconds, between looks too but not while an
entry's command runs, it counts the account's jobs (the user's own count too: the account is also the
user's login). An excess above the cap that lasts KEEPER_CONFIRM (20) seconds (a chain's hand-over lasts
seconds) gives ONE ALERT record per distinct set of job ids: the count, the entries' jobs, ours without an
entry (a run-id name of nrpic-run, <owner>-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS-<commit7>, or an absolute working directory
(squeue %Z) under the repository: a route past the queue), the user's own, and what to do (look, scancel by
hand what should not be there, clear-alert). That record does not halt dispatching: the dispatcher is the
only submitter and submits nothing while the count is at or above the cap, so an excess decays by itself,
and nothing stays stopped after it has gone. When the count is back at or below the cap the keeper logs it;
the next excess is a new record. status shows a standing excess and the user's own jobs ("not ours: ...").

State (untracked): /data/haiyangw/nrpic/locks/queue/ -- entries/<id>.json (one per entry), out/ (output of
each dispatch), queue.log (every change), queue.lock (one flock for every change), submit.lock (held
during a dispatch; nrpic-run checks it), dispatcher.lock (held by the running dispatcher), dispatcher.pid,
dispatcher.json (heartbeat: `status` says HUNG when it is older than three looks), STOP, ALERT, nohup.out.
A restart of `run` resumes from these files.
"""
import calendar
import fcntl
import json
import os
import re
import secrets
import signal
import socket
import subprocess
import sys
import time
import traceback
from contextlib import contextmanager

sys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)), "..", "lib"))
import nrpic_harness as H  # noqa: E402

SCHEMA = "nrpic-queue-entry/1"
OPEN_STATES = ("waiting", "submitting", "submitted", "failed")     # a label is unique among these, per owner
POLL = 120.0
CMD_TIMEOUT = 900.0        # nrpic-run waits up to five minutes for another writer's index.lock
DONE_AFTER = 2             # looks in a row without a job of the entry in squeue
KEEPER = 30.0              # the cap keeper counts the account's jobs this often (seconds), whatever --poll is
KEEPER_CONFIRM = 20.0      # ... and acts only on an excess that lasted this long (a chain's hand-over: seconds)
AGING_HOURS = 8            # a waiting entry's priority improves by one class per this many hours, never past 1
HUNG_LOOKS = 3             # status says HUNG when the heartbeat is older than this many looks
STATE_CHANGING = ("add", "remove", "retry", "mark-done", "run", "stop", "clear-alert")
ORCH_ONLY = ("run", "stop", "clear-alert")
DATA_ROOTS = ("scratch", "kb-data", "cache", "locks", "wt", "runs", ".work")   # as nrpic-ctx
LABEL_RX = re.compile(r"[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]{0,47}")
ID_RX = re.compile(r"q\d{4,}")
RID = r"[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9-]*?-\d{8}-\d{6}-[0-9a-f]{7,40}"
CAP_REFUSAL_RX = re.compile(r"nrpic-run: queue cap:")
DIRTY_REFUSAL_RX = re.compile(r"nrpic-run: (?:the worktree is not clean|not clean where the run's code lives)")
WAIT_CAP = "the queue cap (nrpic-run counted five: a job came in between)"
WAIT_DIRTY = "worktree not clean"
DIRTY_RETRY_LOOKS = 5      # a worktree found not clean is tried again at every fifth look
JOB_RX = re.compile(r"(?:Submitted batch job|submitted job|as Slurm job|: job) (\d+)\b")
START_LINE = ("cd /data/haiyangw/nrpic && mkdir -p locks/queue && setsid nohup /usr/bin/python3 -I "
              "/data/haiyangw/nrpic/harness/bin/nrpic-queue run "
              ">> /data/haiyangw/nrpic/locks/queue/nohup.out 2>&1 < /dev/null &")
STOP_LINE = "cd /data/haiyangw/nrpic && harness/bin/nrpic-queue stop"
TAIL = 4000


def tool_home():
    return H.Worktree(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__))).home


def resolve_worktree(path, home):
    """The worktree holding `path` if it is one of `home`'s and `path` does not lie in a data root of the
    main checkout (scratch/, locks/, ...), else None."""
    try:
        wt = H.Worktree(path)
    except (H.HarnessError, OSError):
        return None
    if wt.home != home:
        return None
    if wt.is_main:
        rel = os.path.relpath(os.path.realpath(path), wt.home)
        if rel.split(os.sep)[0] in DATA_ROOTS:
            return None
    return wt


def cwd_worktree(home):
    try:
        return resolve_worktree(os.getcwd(), home)
    except OSError:
        return None


def acting_worktree(c_opt, strict=True):
    """-C <wt>, else the worktree of the current directory; it must belong to the repository of this
    command. strict: refuse a data root of the main checkout or a directory outside a worktree; otherwise
    fall back to the command's own worktree (read-only commands)."""
    home = tool_home()
    if c_opt:
        wt = resolve_worktree(c_opt, home)
        if wt is None:
            raise H.HarnessError(f"-C {c_opt}: not a worktree of {home} (or it lies in a data root of the main checkout)")
        return wt
    wt = cwd_worktree(home)
    if wt is None:
        if strict:
            raise H.HarnessError(f"the current directory is not inside a worktree of {home} (or lies in a data root "
                                 "of the main checkout): run this from your worktree, or pass -C <worktree>")
        wt = H.Worktree(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)))
    return wt


def epoch(ts):
    try:
        return calendar.timegm(time.strptime(ts, "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ"))
    except (TypeError, ValueError):
        return None


def age(ts, now=None):
    t = epoch(ts)
    if t is None:
        return "-"
    s = max(0, int((now or time.time()) - t))
    if s >= 86400:
        return f"{s // 86400}d{(s % 86400) // 3600:02d}h"
    if s >= 3600:
        return f"{s // 3600}h{(s % 3600) // 60:02d}m"
    return f"{s // 60}m{s % 60:02d}s"


def event(e, what):
    e.setdefault("history", []).append({"ts": H.utcnow(), "event": what})
    del e["history"][:-40]


def pid_alive(pid):
    """The process exists and is not a zombie."""
    try:
        os.kill(int(pid), 0)
    except (OSError, ValueError, TypeError):
        return False
    try:
        return open(f"/proc/{int(pid)}/stat").read().rsplit(")", 1)[1].split()[0] != "Z"
    except (OSError, IndexError):
        return True


def valid_entry(e, eid):
    """An entry file has every field the dispatcher reads (one edited by hand might not: it is skipped and
    reported, so that it cannot stop the queue)."""
    if not isinstance(e, dict) or e.get("id") != eid:
        return False
    strs = ("owner", "label", "state", "worktree", "kind")
    if not all(isinstance(e.get(k), str) and e[k] for k in strs):
        return False
    if not all(isinstance(e.get(k), int) and not isinstance(e.get(k), bool) for k in ("priority", "seq")):
        return False
    if e["kind"] == "submit":
        return isinstance(e.get("argv"), list) and all(isinstance(a, str) for a in e["argv"])
    return e["kind"] == "cmd" and isinstance(e.get("cmd"), str)


def worktree_busy(path):
    """Why the dispatcher should not run a command in this worktree now (a merge, rebase, cherry-pick or
    revert in progress: nrpic-run would find it unclean), or None. index.lock is not a reason: nrpic-run
    waits for it."""
    r = H.run(["git", "-C", path, "rev-parse", "--absolute-git-dir"], check=False)
    if r.returncode != 0:
        return None                       # the command itself then fails and says why
    gd = r.stdout.strip()
    for f, what in (("MERGE_HEAD", "a merge"), ("rebase-merge", "a rebase"), ("rebase-apply", "a rebase"),
                    ("CHERRY_PICK_HEAD", "a cherry-pick"), ("REVERT_HEAD", "a revert")):
        if os.path.exists(os.path.join(gd, f)):
            return f"worktree in the middle of {what}"
    return None


def set_wait(x, what, detail=None, tried=False):
    """Record in entry x why it waits (list, show and status show it). `since` stays while the reason stays;
    tried: the entry's command ran and was refused for this reason. Returns True when x changed."""
    w = dict(x.get("wait") or {})
    if w.get("what") != what:
        w = {"what": what, "since": H.utcnow(), "tries": 0}
        event(x, f"waits: {what}")
    elif not tried and (detail is None or w.get("detail") == detail):
        return False
    if detail is not None:
        w["detail"] = detail
    if tried:
        w["tries"] = w.get("tries", 0) + 1
        w["last_try"] = H.utcnow()
    x["wait"] = w
    return True


def wait_text(e):
    w = e.get("wait") or {}
    if not w.get("what"):
        return ""
    return f"waits: {w['what']} since {w.get('since')}" + (f" ({w['tries']} tries)" if w.get("tries") else "")


def first_line(*texts):
    """The first line of the first text that has one, skipping nrpic-run's notes (`nrpic-run: note: ...`)."""
    for t in texts:
        for ln in (t or "").splitlines():
            s = ln.strip()
            if s and not s.startswith("nrpic-run: note:"):
                return s[:400]
    return ""


# ------------------------------------------------------------------ the state directory

class Queue:
    def __init__(self, home):
        self.home = home
        self.dir = H.queue_dir(home)
        self.edir = os.path.join(self.dir, "entries")
        self.odir = os.path.join(self.dir, "out")
        self.bad = []

    def ensure(self):
        for d in (self.dir, self.edir, self.odir):
            os.makedirs(d, exist_ok=True)
        return self

    def path(self, name):
        return os.path.join(self.dir, name)

    @contextmanager
    def lock(self):
        self.ensure()
        with open(self.path("queue.lock"), "a") as f:
            fcntl.flock(f, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
            try:
                yield
            finally:
                fcntl.flock(f, fcntl.LOCK_UN)

    def entry_path(self, eid):
        return os.path.join(self.edir, eid + ".json")

    def load(self, eid):
        if not ID_RX.fullmatch(eid or ""):
            raise H.HarnessError(f"{eid!r} is not an entry id (q0001, ...)")
        p = self.entry_path(eid)
        if not os.path.isfile(p):
            raise H.HarnessError(f"no entry {eid} in {self.edir}")
        return H.read_json(p)

    def entries(self):
        """Every entry, in the order of adding. A file that cannot be read is listed in .bad and skipped."""
        out, self.bad = [], []
        if not os.path.isdir(self.edir):
            return out
        for fn in sorted(os.listdir(self.edir)):
            m = re.fullmatch(r"(q\d{4,})\.json", fn)
            if not m:
                continue
            try:
                e = H.read_json(os.path.join(self.edir, fn))
            except (OSError, ValueError) as ex:
                self.bad.append((fn, repr(ex)))
                continue
            if valid_entry(e, m.group(1)):
                out.append(e)
            else:
                self.bad.append((fn, "not an entry of this queue (fields missing or of the wrong type)"))
        out.sort(key=lambda e: (e.get("seq", 0), e["id"]))
        return out

    def save(self, e):
        e["updated"] = H.utcnow()
        H.write_json(self.entry_path(e["id"]), e)

    def change(self, eid, fn):
        """fn(entry) under the lock, on the entry as it is on disk; saved unless fn returns False.
        Returns the entry as saved, or None when fn declined."""
        with self.lock():
            e = self.load(eid)
            if fn(e) is False:
                return None
            self.save(e)
            return e

    def new_id(self):
        """The next entry id (call under the lock)."""
        p = self.path("next_id")
        try:
            n = int(open(p).read().strip())
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            n = 1
        while os.path.exists(self.entry_path(f"q{n:04d}")):
            n += 1
        with open(p + ".tmp", "w") as f:
            f.write(f"{n + 1}\n")
        os.replace(p + ".tmp", p)
        return f"q{n:04d}", n

    def next_dispatch_no(self):
        return max([e.get("dispatch_no") or 0 for e in self.entries()] + [0]) + 1

    def log(self, msg, loud=False):
        self.ensure()
        line = f"{H.utcnow()} {msg}\n"
        with open(self.path("queue.log"), "a") as f:
            f.write(line)
        if loud:
            sys.stderr.write(line)
            sys.stderr.flush()

    def dispatcher(self):
        """{alive, pid, started, last_look, poll, state} of the dispatcher."""
        info = {}
        try:
            info = H.read_json(self.path("dispatcher.json"))
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            pass
        pid = None
        try:
            pid = int(open(self.path("dispatcher.pid")).read().strip())
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            pass
        alive = False
        if pid and pid_alive(pid) and info.get("host", socket.gethostname()) == socket.gethostname():
            try:
                cmdline = open(f"/proc/{pid}/cmdline", "rb").read().replace(b"\0", b" ").decode(errors="replace")
            except OSError:
                cmdline = ""
            alive = "nrpic-queue" in cmdline and " run" in cmdline
        info.update(pid=pid, alive=alive)
        return info


# ------------------------------------------------------------------ order and done

def blocked_reason(e, by_id):
    """None when a waiting entry may be dispatched now (as far as --after goes), else why it waits."""
    aid = e.get("after_id")
    if not aid:
        return None
    a = by_id.get(aid)
    if a is None:
        return f"after {e.get('after')}: entry {aid} is missing"
    if a["state"] == "done":
        return None
    if a["state"] in ("failed", "removed"):
        return f"after {a['label']} ({aid}), which {a['state'] == 'failed' and 'failed' or 'was removed'}: " \
               f"retry it, or remove {e['id']}"
    return f"after {a['label']} ({aid}, {a['state']})"


def eff_priority(e, now=None):
    """The priority the dispatcher uses: a waiting entry improves by one class for every AGING_HOURS since it
    was added, never past 1 (0 and 1 are given only by the orchestrator), so that nothing starves."""
    p = e["priority"]
    t = epoch(e.get("added"))
    if p <= 1 or t is None:
        return p
    return max(1, p - int(max(0.0, (now or time.time()) - t) // (AGING_HOURS * 3600)))


def dispatch_order(entries, now=None):
    """The waiting entries that may be dispatched now, in the order the dispatcher takes them: lowest
    effective priority first (eff_priority); within it the owner served longest ago (never served first;
    then the earliest added); within an owner the order of adding. Serving an entry counts for its owner."""
    by_id = {e["id"]: e for e in entries}
    now = now or time.time()
    served = {}
    for e in entries:
        n = e.get("dispatch_no")
        if isinstance(n, int):
            served[e["owner"]] = max(served.get(e["owner"], 0), n)
    nxt = max(served.values(), default=0) + 1
    pool = [e for e in entries if e["state"] == "waiting" and blocked_reason(e, by_id) is None]
    prio = {e["id"]: eff_priority(e, now) for e in pool}
    out = []
    while pool:
        p = min(prio[e["id"]] for e in pool)
        heads = {}
        for e in pool:
            if prio[e["id"]] == p and e["owner"] not in heads:
                heads[e["owner"]] = e
        pick = min(heads.values(), key=lambda x: (served.get(x["owner"], 0), x["seq"]))
        out.append(pick)
        pool.remove(pick)
        served[pick["owner"]] = nxt
        nxt += 1
    return out


def entry_name(e):
    """The job name by which an entry's jobs are known, only when it is the entry's own run id (unique; a
    chain resubmits itself under it); never a generic name such as `batch`."""
    n = e.get("job_name")
    return n if n and n == e.get("run_id") else None


def owns_job(e, j):
    """Is job j (or array task) the entry's: by job id first (recorded at its dispatch), else by its run-id name."""
    return printed_by(j["id"], [str(x) for x in e.get("job_ids") or []]) or bool(
        entry_name(e) and j["name"] == entry_name(e))


def job_live(e, jobs):
    return any(owns_job(e, j) for j in jobs)


def classify_jobs(jobs, entries, home):
    """[(job, kind, detail)] for the jobs of the account: "entry" (detail: the entry's id; by job id, or by the
    entry's own run-id name), "ours" (no entry, but a run-id name or a working directory under the repository:
    a route past the queue; detail: which), "user" (the user's own)."""
    held = [e for e in entries if e["state"] in ("submitted", "failed", "submitting")]
    out = []
    for j in jobs:
        e = next((x for x in held if printed_by(j["id"], [str(i) for i in x.get("job_ids") or []])), None) or \
            next((x for x in held if entry_name(x) and j["name"] == entry_name(x)), None)
        if e is not None:
            out.append((j, "entry", e["id"]))
        else:
            why = H.program_job(j, home)
            out.append((j, "ours" if why else "user", why))
    return out


def chain_status(home, e):
    if not e.get("run_id"):
        return None
    p = os.path.join(home, "scratch", e["owner"], e["run_id"], "chain", "STATUS")
    try:
        return open(p).read().strip() or None
    except OSError:
        return None


def track_done(Q, jobs):
    """Submitted entries none of whose jobs (by name, then by id) is in squeue at DONE_AFTER looks in a
    row become done. Returns the entries marked done."""
    done = []
    for e in Q.entries():
        if e["state"] != "submitted":
            continue
        live = job_live(e, jobs)

        def upd(x, live=live):
            if x["state"] != "submitted":
                return False
            if live:
                if x.get("absent_looks"):
                    x["absent_looks"] = 0
                    return True
                return False
            x["absent_looks"] = x.get("absent_looks", 0) + 1
            if x["absent_looks"] < DONE_AFTER:
                return True
            x["state"] = "done"
            x["ended"] = H.utcnow()
            cs = chain_status(Q.home, x)
            if cs:
                x["chain_status"] = cs
            how = (f"job name {x['job_name']}" if x.get("job_name") else
                   f"job id {', '.join(x['job_ids'])}" if x.get("job_ids") else "no job of it was ever identified")
            if cs in ("QUEUED", "RUNNING"):
                how += f"; its chain/STATUS still says {cs} (its job ended without the chain closing it)"
            event(x, f"done: not in squeue at {DONE_AFTER} looks in a row ({how})")
            return True
        x = Q.change(e["id"], upd)
        if x is not None and x["state"] == "done":
            done.append(x)
            Q.log(f"done {x['id']} {x['owner']}/{x['label']}: {x['history'][-1]['event']}")
    return done


# ------------------------------------------------------------------ a dispatch

def command_of(e):
    if e["kind"] == "submit":
        return [sys.executable, "-I", os.path.join(e["worktree"], "harness", "bin", "nrpic-run"), "submit"] + \
            list(e["argv"])
    return ["/bin/bash", "-c", e["cmd"]]


def describe(e):
    if e["kind"] == "submit":
        return "nrpic-run submit " + " ".join(e["argv"])
    return e["cmd"]


def parse_output(text):
    """(run id or None, [job ids]) printed by nrpic-run, scripts/submit_chain.sh, gpu_batch.sh or sbatch."""
    run_id = None
    m = re.search(rf"\b(?:submitted|registered) ({RID})\b", text)
    if m:
        run_id = m.group(1)
    if run_id is None:
        m = re.search(r"chain started in (\S+): job \d+", text)
        if m and re.fullmatch(RID, os.path.basename(m.group(1).rstrip("/"))):
            run_id = os.path.basename(m.group(1).rstrip("/"))
    found = JOB_RX.findall(text) or [ln.strip() for ln in text.splitlines() if re.fullmatch(r"\s*\d+\s*", ln)]
    jobs = []
    for j in found:                       # a line of digits alone (sbatch --parsable) only when nothing else says
        if j not in jobs:
            jobs.append(j)
    return run_id, jobs


def printed_by(jid, printed):
    """Is job (or array task) `jid` one of the job ids a command printed?"""
    return any(jid == p or jid.startswith(p + "_") for p in printed)


def fresh_jobs(before, after, printed=()):
    """(fresh, successors) among the jobs in `after` whose id was not in `before`. A successor is a chain's
    next segment: its id was not printed by the command, it carries the name of a job listed before as not
    pending (the running segment that resubmits), and each such name has at most one. Every other new job is
    fresh: a job the command printed always is."""
    bids = {j["id"] for j in before}
    running = {j["name"] for j in before if j["name"] and j["state"] != "PENDING"}
    fresh, succ, taken = [], [], set()
    for j in after:
        if j["id"] in bids:
            continue
        if not printed_by(j["id"], printed) and j["name"] in running and j["name"] not in taken:
            taken.add(j["name"])
            succ.append(j)
        else:
            fresh.append(j)
    return fresh, succ


def alert_halts(path):
    """Does the ALERT file halt dispatching? Every record does (an unreadable file too), except the cap keeper's
    reports of an excess (halts: false)."""
    try:
        a = H.read_json(path)
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return True
    if not isinstance(a, dict):
        return True
    return any(not isinstance(r, dict) or r.get("halts", True) for r in [a] + list(a.get("more") or []))


def jobs_of_outcome(text, before, after):
    """(run id, job ids, job name) of what a command submitted, recorded on every outcome. Job ids: those it
    printed that are new at this dispatch (not listed before it; array tasks of a printed id included), else
    the one new job that appeared (not a chain's next segment). Job name: only the entry's own run id, when
    the command printed one and its jobs carry it (nrpic-run names a job after its run id); never a generic
    name, which another job may carry too."""
    run_id, printed = parse_output(text)
    bids = {j["id"] for j in before or []}
    jids = [p for p in printed if p not in bids and not any(b.startswith(p + "_") for b in bids)]
    fresh = fresh_jobs(before, after, printed)[0] if after is not None and before is not None else []
    if not jids and len(fresh) == 1:
        jids = [fresh[0]["id"]]
    listed = [j for j in after or [] if printed_by(j["id"], jids)]
    name = run_id if run_id and (not listed or any(j["name"] == run_id for j in listed)) else None
    return run_id, jids, name


def tail(s, n=TAIL):
    s = (s or "").strip()
    return s if len(s) <= n else "..." + s[-n:]


def read_tail(path, n=1 << 20):
    """The last n bytes of a file as text ('' when it cannot be read)."""
    try:
        with open(path, "rb") as f:
            f.seek(0, os.SEEK_END)
            f.seek(max(0, f.tell() - n))
            return f.read().decode("utf-8", "replace")
    except OSError:
        return ""


def proc_start(pid):
    """The start time (clock ticks after boot) of a process, or None: with it a process group recorded in an
    entry is told apart from a later one that got the same number."""
    try:
        return int(open(f"/proc/{int(pid)}/stat").read().rsplit(")", 1)[1].split()[19])
    except (OSError, ValueError, IndexError):
        return None


def group_alive(pgid):
    try:
        os.killpg(int(pgid), 0)
        return True
    except ProcessLookupError:
        return False
    except (PermissionError, OSError):
        return True


def end_group(pgid, term_wait=10.0, kill_wait=20.0, child=None):
    """SIGTERM, then SIGKILL, the process group pgid, waiting until none of its processes is left. child: the
    group's leader when it is this process's own child (a Popen), reaped while waiting: a zombie still counts
    as a member of its group. Returns True when the group is gone."""
    def alive():
        if child is not None:
            child.poll()
        return group_alive(pgid)
    for sig, wait in ((signal.SIGTERM, term_wait), (signal.SIGKILL, kill_wait)):
        try:
            os.killpg(int(pgid), sig)
        except ProcessLookupError:
            return True
        except OSError:
            pass
        t_end = time.time() + wait
        while time.time() < t_end:
            if not alive():
                return True
            time.sleep(0.1)
    return not alive()


def jobkey(j):
    """Order of submission of a job or array task (Slurm job ids increase): 123 < 123_4 < 124."""
    m = re.fullmatch(r"(\d+)(?:_(\d+))?", j["id"])
    return (int(m.group(1)), int(m.group(2) or -1)) if m else (0, 0)


class Dispatcher:
    def __init__(self, wt, poll, cmd_timeout, keeper=KEEPER, keeper_confirm=KEEPER_CONFIRM):
        self.wt = wt
        self.Q = Queue(wt.home).ensure()
        self.env = H.build_env(wt)
        self.poll = poll
        self.cmd_timeout = cmd_timeout
        self.keeper = keeper
        self.keeper_confirm = keeper_confirm
        self.term = False
        self.why = None                 # the last reason logged for not submitting
        self.pause_seen = False
        self.bad_seen = set()
        self.started = H.utcnow()
        self.last_look = None
        self.state = "running"
        self.beat_t = 0.0
        self.beat_failed = False
        self.last_keep = 0.0
        self.over_since = None          # time of the first of the counts in a row above the cap
        self.last_reported = None       # the job ids of the last excess reported (one record per set)
        self.in_excess = False          # the count is above the cap (its end is logged)

    # -- small things
    def say(self, key, msg):
        """Log why nothing is submitted, once per change of the reason."""
        if self.why != key:
            self.why = key
            self.Q.log(msg)

    def stopping(self):
        return self.term or os.path.exists(self.Q.path("STOP"))

    def on_term(self, signum, frame):
        self.term = True

    def heartbeat(self, state=None, look=False):
        """dispatcher.json: pid, host, the time of this beat and of the last look. A failing write is logged
        once and does not stop the dispatcher."""
        if state:
            self.state = state
        if look:
            self.last_look = H.utcnow()
        self.beat_t = time.time()
        try:
            H.write_json(self.Q.path("dispatcher.json"),
                         {"pid": os.getpid(), "host": socket.gethostname(), "started": self.started,
                          "beat": H.utcnow(), "last_look": self.last_look, "poll": self.poll, "keeper": self.keeper,
                          "cap": H.QUEUE_CAP, "state": self.state})
            self.beat_failed = False
        except OSError as ex:
            if not self.beat_failed:
                self.beat_failed = True
                self.Q.log(f"WARNING: the heartbeat could not be written: {ex}", loud=True)

    def beat(self):
        if time.time() - self.beat_t >= min(5.0, self.poll):
            self.heartbeat()

    def note_pause(self):
        p = os.path.exists(os.path.join(self.Q.home, "locks", "PAUSE"))
        if p != self.pause_seen:
            self.pause_seen = p
            self.Q.log("the pause flag locks/PAUSE exists: card submissions go on (decision 0026 item 2)" if p
                       else "the pause flag locks/PAUSE is gone")

    def sleep(self):
        """Until the next look; the cap keeper counts meanwhile every --keeper seconds."""
        end = time.time() + self.poll
        while not self.stopping():
            left = end - time.time()
            if left <= 0:
                return
            if time.time() - self.last_keep >= self.keeper:
                try:
                    self.keep()
                except Exception as ex:          # logged; the dispatcher goes on
                    self.Q.log(f"error in the cap keeper: {type(ex).__name__}: {ex}", loud=True)
            self.beat()
            time.sleep(min(1.0, left, max(0.05, self.keeper)))

    # -- the loop
    def run(self):
        lockf = open(self.Q.path("dispatcher.lock"), "a")
        try:
            fcntl.flock(lockf, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
        except OSError:
            d = self.Q.dispatcher()
            raise H.HarnessError(f"a dispatcher is already running (pid {d.get('pid')}, last beat "
                                 f"{d.get('beat')}); stop it first: {STOP_LINE}")
        stop = self.Q.path("STOP")
        try:
            os.chdir(self.wt.home)               # never hold a working directory inside a worktree
            if os.path.exists(stop):
                os.remove(stop)
                self.Q.log("removed a STOP file left from before (no dispatcher was running)")
            with open(self.Q.path("dispatcher.pid"), "w") as f:
                f.write(f"{os.getpid()}\n")
            signal.signal(signal.SIGTERM, self.on_term)
            signal.signal(signal.SIGINT, self.on_term)
            signal.signal(signal.SIGHUP, signal.SIG_IGN)
            self.heartbeat()
            self.Q.log(f"dispatcher start: pid {os.getpid()} on {socket.gethostname()}, a look every {self.poll:g} s, "
                       f"the cap keeper every {self.keeper:g} s (acting on an excess of {self.keeper_confirm:g} s), "
                       f"cap {H.QUEUE_CAP} jobs of the account (decision 0033), state {self.Q.dir}")
            self.recover()
            while not self.stopping():
                try:
                    self.keep()                  # the cap keeper at every look
                    self.look()
                    self.heartbeat(look=True)
                except Exception as ex:          # the dispatcher outlives a transient error; it is logged
                    self.Q.log(f"error at a look (the dispatcher goes on): {type(ex).__name__}: {ex}", loud=True)
                    traceback.print_exc()
                self.sleep()
        finally:
            how = "STOP file" if os.path.exists(stop) else "signal" if self.term else "error"
            self.Q.log(f"dispatcher exit ({how}): pid {os.getpid()}")
            try:
                if open(self.Q.path("dispatcher.pid")).read().strip() == str(os.getpid()):
                    os.remove(self.Q.path("dispatcher.pid"))
            except OSError:
                pass
            if os.path.exists(stop):
                os.remove(stop)
            self.heartbeat("stopped")
            fcntl.flock(lockf, fcntl.LOCK_UN)
            lockf.close()
        return 0

    def recover(self):
        """An entry left `submitting` by a dispatcher that ended: its command may still run (its process group
        is ended here, and waited for, before the first look) and may have submitted a job (what its output
        shows is recorded). It is marked failed and never run again by itself."""
        for e in self.Q.entries():
            if e["state"] != "submitting":
                continue
            how, gone = "no process group was recorded", True
            pg = e.get("pgid")
            base = os.path.join(self.Q.odir, f"{e['id']}.{e.get('attempts', 1)}")
            if not pg:                           # killed between the fork and the save: the child wrote it itself
                try:
                    pg = int(open(base + ".pgid").read().strip())
                except (OSError, ValueError):
                    pg = None
            if pg and e.get("pg_host") not in (None, socket.gethostname()):
                how, gone = f"its process group {pg} was on host {e['pg_host']}", False
            elif pg and not group_alive(pg):
                how = f"its process group {pg} had ended"
            elif pg and e.get("pg_start") is not None and proc_start(pg) not in (None, e["pg_start"]):
                how = f"process group {pg} belongs to another program now (left alone)"
            elif pg:
                gone = end_group(pg)
                how = f"its process group {pg} was {'ended' if gone else 'NOT ended (still alive after SIGKILL)'}"
            text = read_tail(base + ".stdout") + "\n" + read_tail(base + ".stderr")
            run_id, jids = parse_output(text)
            jname = run_id                       # a job is known by name only by the entry's own run id

            def upd(x):
                if x["state"] != "submitting":
                    return False
                x["state"] = "failed"
                x["error"] = (f"the dispatcher ended while this entry's command ran (from {x.get('dispatch_started')}); "
                              f"{how}. It may have submitted a job (recorded if it printed one): look at squeue and "
                              f"`nrpic-run status` in {x['worktree']}, then `nrpic-queue retry {x['id']}` (nothing was "
                              f"submitted) or `nrpic-queue mark-done {x['id']}` (its job has ended)")
                x["error_line"] = f"the dispatcher ended while its command ran; {how}"
                x["run_id"], x["job_ids"], x["job_name"] = run_id, jids, jname
                x.pop("dispatch_token", None)
                x["dispatch_no"] = self.Q.next_dispatch_no()
                event(x, f"failed at restart: was submitting; {how}")
                return True
            if self.Q.change(e["id"], upd):
                self.Q.log(f"FAILED {e['id']} {e['owner']}/{e['label']}: was submitting when the dispatcher ended; {how}"
                           + (f"; it printed job(s) {', '.join(jids)}" if jids else ""), loud=True)
            if not gone:
                self.raise_alert({"ts": H.utcnow(), "kind": "leftover-command", "entry": e["id"], "owner": e["owner"],
                                  "label": e["label"], "pgid": pg, "what": how},
                                 f"the command of {e['id']} left by the dispatcher before could not be ended ({how})")

    def look(self):
        jobs = H.queue_jobs(self.env)
        if jobs is not None:
            track_done(self.Q, jobs)
        self.note_pause()
        while not self.stopping():
            if os.path.exists(self.Q.path("ALERT")) and alert_halts(self.Q.path("ALERT")):
                self.say("alert", "ALERT present (locks/queue/ALERT): nothing is submitted until the orchestrator "
                                  "runs `nrpic-queue clear-alert`")
                return
            jobs = H.queue_jobs(self.env)
            if jobs is None:
                self.say("squeue", "squeue did not answer: nothing is submitted at this look")
                return
            ents = self.Q.entries()
            for fn, why in self.Q.bad:
                if fn not in self.bad_seen:
                    self.bad_seen.add(fn)
                    self.Q.log(f"WARNING: skipped {os.path.join(self.Q.edir, fn)}: {why}", loud=True)
            order = dispatch_order(ents)
            free, held = self.ready(order)
            if order and not free:
                self.say("held:" + "; ".join(held), f"{len(order)} {'entry waits' if len(order) == 1 else 'entries wait'}"
                                                    f" for their worktrees: {'; '.join(held)}")
                return
            order = free
            if not order:
                nw = sum(e["state"] == "waiting" for e in ents)
                self.say(f"idle{nw}", ("nothing waits" if nw == 0 else f"{nw} waiting, all blocked by --after")
                         + f"; {len(jobs)} of {H.QUEUE_CAP} jobs of the account queued")
                return
            if len(jobs) >= H.QUEUE_CAP:
                self.say("cap", f"{len(jobs)} of {H.QUEUE_CAP} jobs of the account queued: {len(order)} "
                                f"{'entry waits' if len(order) == 1 else 'entries wait'} "
                                f"(next {order[0]['id']} {order[0]['owner']}/{order[0]['label']})")
                return
            e = self.claim(order[0])
            if e is None:
                continue                         # removed meanwhile
            try:
                with self.submit_lock():         # from the count before, through the command, to the count after
                    before = H.queue_jobs(self.env)  # counted again immediately before the submission
                    if before is None or len(before) >= H.QUEUE_CAP:
                        self.unclaim(e)
                        self.say("cap", f"{'squeue did not answer' if before is None else f'{len(before)} of {H.QUEUE_CAP} jobs queued'}"
                                        f" at the count before {e['id']}: back to waiting")
                        return
                    self.why = None
                    res = self.dispatch(e, before)
            except BaseException as ex:          # never leave an entry `submitting` behind
                self.fail_if_submitting(e, ex)
                raise
            if res != "go-on":
                return

    def fail_if_submitting(self, e, ex):
        line = traceback.format_exception_only(type(ex), ex)[-1].strip()
        try:
            cur = self.Q.load(e["id"])
            if cur.get("state") == "submitting" and cur.get("pgid") and group_alive(cur["pgid"]):
                end_group(cur["pgid"], 5.0, 5.0)
        except (H.HarnessError, OSError, ValueError):
            cur = None

        def upd(x):
            if x["state"] != "submitting":
                return False
            x["state"] = "failed"
            x["error"] = f"an error of the dispatcher during the dispatch: {line}"
            x["error_line"] = line
            x.pop("dispatch_token", None)
            x["dispatch_no"] = self.Q.next_dispatch_no()
            event(x, f"failed: an error of the dispatcher: {line[:200]}")
            return True
        try:
            if self.Q.change(e["id"], upd):
                self.Q.log(f"FAILED {e['id']} {e['owner']}/{e['label']}: an error of the dispatcher during the "
                           f"dispatch: {line}", loud=True)
        except (H.HarnessError, OSError, ValueError):
            pass

    def ready(self, order):
        """(the entries of `order` whose worktree may take a command now, the reasons the others wait). A
        worktree in the middle of a merge or rebase holds its entries back (recorded as their wait, cleared when
        it is over); an entry whose worktree nrpic-run found not clean is tried again every DIRTY_RETRY_LOOKS."""
        free, held, busy, now = [], [], {}, time.time()
        for cand in order:
            wt = cand["worktree"]
            if wt not in busy:
                busy[wt] = worktree_busy(wt)
            w = cand.get("wait") or {}
            if busy[wt]:
                self.Q.change(cand["id"], lambda x, b=busy[wt]: x["state"] == "waiting" and set_wait(x, b))
                held.append(f"{cand['id']}: {busy[wt]}")
                continue
            if str(w.get("what", "")).startswith("worktree in the middle of"):
                self.Q.change(cand["id"], lambda x: x["state"] == "waiting" and bool(x.pop("wait", None)))
            if w.get("what") == WAIT_DIRTY and (epoch(w.get("last_try")) or 0) > now - DIRTY_RETRY_LOOKS * self.poll:
                held.append(f"{cand['id']}: {WAIT_DIRTY} (tried again at a later look)")
                continue
            free.append(cand)
        return free, held

    @contextmanager
    def submit_lock(self):
        with open(H.queue_submit_lock(self.Q.home), "a") as f:
            fcntl.flock(f, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
            try:
                yield
            finally:
                fcntl.flock(f, fcntl.LOCK_UN)

    def claim(self, e):
        def upd(x):
            if x["state"] != "waiting":
                return False
            x["state"] = "submitting"
            x["attempts"] = x.get("attempts", 0) + 1
            x["dispatch_started"] = H.utcnow()
            x["dispatch_token"] = secrets.token_hex(12)   # nrpic-run checks it against the marker
            for k in ("pgid", "pg_start", "pg_host"):
                x.pop(k, None)
            event(x, f"dispatch attempt {x['attempts']}")
            return True
        return self.Q.change(e["id"], upd)

    def unclaim(self, e):
        def upd(x):
            if x["state"] != "submitting":
                return False
            x["state"] = "waiting"
            x["attempts"] = max(0, x.get("attempts", 1) - 1)
            x.pop("dispatch_token", None)
            event(x, "back to waiting: the queue was full at the count before the submission")
            return True
        self.Q.change(e["id"], upd)

    def execute(self, e):
        """Run the entry's command in its worktree, its output into files (out/<id>.<n>.stdout, .stderr; never
        pipes, so that a child left behind cannot hold the dispatcher), its process group recorded in the entry
        (a restart ends it); wait at most --cmd-timeout; end what is left of its process group afterwards.
        Returns (exit status or None, stdout, stderr, timed out, the log out/<id>.<n>.log)."""
        wt = H.Worktree(e["worktree"])
        if wt.owner != e["owner"]:
            raise H.HarnessError(f"{e['worktree']} is now on branch {wt.branch} (owner {wt.owner}), not {e['owner']}'s")
        # the marker of the one route (decision 0033): nrpic-run lets a card submission through only with it,
        # and still applies the cap; a --cmd wrapper that calls nrpic-run inside inherits it
        env = H.build_env(wt, extra={H.QUEUE_DISPATCH_VAR: f"{e['id']}:{e['dispatch_token']}"})
        argv = command_of(e)
        n = e.get("attempts", 1)
        base = os.path.join(self.Q.odir, f"{e['id']}.{n}")
        t0 = time.time()
        pgfile = base + ".pgid"

        def note_group():                        # in the child, after setsid, before exec: a restart finds the group
            with open(pgfile, "w") as f:         # even when the dispatcher dies between the fork and the save below
                f.write(f"{os.getpid()}\n")
        with open(base + ".stdout", "w") as fo, open(base + ".stderr", "w") as fe:
            p = subprocess.Popen(argv, cwd=wt.root, env=env, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, stdout=fo, stderr=fe,
                                 start_new_session=True, preexec_fn=note_group)
        start = proc_start(p.pid)
        self.Q.change(e["id"], lambda x: x["state"] == "submitting" and (
            x.update(pgid=p.pid, pg_start=start, pg_host=socket.gethostname()) or True))
        timed_out = False
        while True:
            try:
                p.wait(timeout=1.0)
                break
            except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
                self.beat()
                if time.time() - t0 >= self.cmd_timeout:
                    timed_out = True
                    end_group(p.pid, 30.0, 10.0, child=p)
                    try:
                        p.wait(timeout=10.0)
                    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
                        pass
                    break
        rc = p.returncode
        left = group_alive(p.pid)
        if left:                                 # children it left behind may not submit later
            end_group(p.pid, child=p)
        out, err = read_tail(base + ".stdout"), read_tail(base + ".stderr")
        logp = base + ".log"
        with open(logp, "w") as f:
            f.write(f"# {e['id']} {e['owner']}/{e['label']} attempt {n} at {e.get('dispatch_started')}\n"
                    f"# cwd {wt.root}\n# argv {json.dumps(argv)}\n# exit {rc}{' (timed out)' if timed_out else ''} "
                    f"after {time.time() - t0:.1f} s" + ("; processes it left in its group were ended" if left else "")
                    + f"\n--- stdout\n{out}\n--- stderr\n{err}\n")
        return rc, out, err, timed_out, logp

    def dispatch(self, e, before):
        """Run one claimed entry's command (the caller holds the submit lock); record the outcome and what it
        submitted, on every outcome; check the rise of the count. Returns "go-on" when the dispatcher may go on
        at this look, else ends the look."""
        eid = e["id"]
        try:
            rc, out, err, timed_out, logp = self.execute(e)
        except Exception as ex:
            msg = f"could not run the command: {type(ex).__name__}: {ex}"
            self.fail(e, msg, None, None, msg)
            return "go-on"
        after = H.queue_jobs(self.env)
        text = out + "\n" + err
        printed = parse_output(text)[1]
        run_id, jids, name = jobs_of_outcome(text, before, after)
        outcome = "go-on"
        refusal = None if rc == 0 or timed_out else (
            WAIT_CAP if CAP_REFUSAL_RX.search(text) else WAIT_DIRTY if DIRTY_REFUSAL_RX.search(text) else None)
        if refusal and printed:
            refusal = None                       # it had submitted something first: a failure, its jobs recorded
        if refusal:
            m = (CAP_REFUSAL_RX if refusal == WAIT_CAP else DIRTY_REFUSAL_RX).search(text)
            detail = "\n".join(text[m.start():].splitlines()[:8])

            def upd(x):
                x["state"] = "waiting"
                x.pop("dispatch_token", None)
                x["refusals"] = x.get("refusals", 0) + 1
                x["last_refusal"] = tail(detail, 1200)
                set_wait(x, refusal, tail(detail, 1200), tried=True)
                event(x, f"refused by nrpic-run ({refusal}): back to waiting")
                return True
            x = self.Q.change(eid, upd)
            if refusal == WAIT_CAP or (x and x["wait"]["tries"] == 1):
                self.Q.log(f"refused {eid} {e['owner']}/{e['label']} by nrpic-run ({refusal}): back to waiting"
                           + ("" if refusal == WAIT_CAP else f", tried again every {DIRTY_RETRY_LOOKS}th look")
                           + f" ({logp})")
            outcome = "refused" if refusal == WAIT_CAP else "go-on"
        elif rc == 0 and not timed_out:
            others = [x for x in self.Q.entries() if x["id"] != eid and x["state"] == "submitted"]
            claimed = [j for j in jids if any(printed_by(j, [str(i) for i in x.get("job_ids") or []]) for x in others)]
            if claimed or (name and any(entry_name(x) == name for x in others)):
                self.Q.log(f"WARNING: {eid}: job(s) {claimed or '-'} or the name {name} belong to another submitted "
                           "entry already; not taken for this one (two entries never claim one job)", loud=True)
                jids = [j for j in jids if j not in claimed]
                name = None if name and any(entry_name(x) == name for x in others) else name

            def upd(x):
                x["state"] = "submitted"
                x["submitted"] = H.utcnow()
                x.pop("dispatch_token", None)
                x.pop("wait", None)
                x["run_id"], x["job_ids"], x["job_name"] = run_id, jids, name
                x["absent_looks"] = 0
                x["dispatch_no"] = self.Q.next_dispatch_no()
                x["stdout_tail"] = tail(out, 1500)
                x["output_log"] = logp
                event(x, f"submitted: run {run_id or '-'}, job {', '.join(jids) or '-'}, job name {name or '-'}")
                return True
            x = self.Q.change(eid, upd)
            self.Q.log(f"submitted {eid} {e['owner']}/{e['label']} (p{e['priority']}): run {run_id or '-'}, "
                       f"job {', '.join(jids) or '-'}, name {name or '-'}; "
                       f"{len(after) if after is not None else '?'} of {H.QUEUE_CAP} jobs queued")
            if not name and not jids:
                self.Q.log(f"note: {eid}: its command exited 0 but no job of it was identified; it will be marked "
                           f"done at the next looks ({logp})")
            e = x or e
        else:
            why = (f"timed out after {self.cmd_timeout:g} s and was ended" if timed_out else f"exit status {rc}")
            if jids:
                why += f"; it submitted job(s) {', '.join(jids)} (recorded: retry and mark-done wait until they end)"
            self.fail(e, f"{why}: {tail(err or out, 2000)}", rc, logp, first_line(err, out) or why,
                      (run_id, jids, name))
        # the rise of the account's count: at most one job per entry (decision 0033)
        if after is None:
            self.Q.log(f"WARNING: squeue did not answer after {eid}: the rise of the count was not checked; nothing "
                       "more is submitted at this look", loud=True)
            return "stop"
        fresh, succ = fresh_jobs(before, after, printed)
        # strict: every job of the account that is new around the dispatch counts for it (a job the user
        # submits by hand in those seconds too), unless it is a chain's next segment
        if len(fresh) > 1:
            self.alert(e, before, after, fresh, succ, printed)
            return "stop"
        if len(after) > H.QUEUE_CAP:
            self.Q.log(f"WARNING: {len(after)} jobs of the account are queued, above the cap of {H.QUEUE_CAP} "
                       f"(new since the count before {eid}: {[j['id'] + ' ' + j['name'] for j in fresh + succ]}; a "
                       "chain hands over to its next segment with both listed for seconds; the cap keeper acts on "
                       "an excess that lasts)", loud=True)
        return outcome

    def fail(self, e, error, rc, logp, line=None, jobs=None):
        def upd(x):
            x["state"] = "failed"
            x["error"] = error
            x["error_line"] = line or first_line(error)      # the first line of its stderr, shown by list
            x["exit_code"] = rc
            x.pop("dispatch_token", None)
            x.pop("wait", None)
            if jobs is not None:                 # what it submitted before it failed (retry and mark-done wait)
                x["run_id"], x["job_ids"], x["job_name"] = jobs
            x["output_log"] = logp
            x["dispatch_no"] = self.Q.next_dispatch_no()
            event(x, f"failed: {error[:200]}")
            return True
        self.Q.change(e["id"], upd)
        self.Q.log(f"FAILED {e['id']} {e['owner']}/{e['label']}: {error[:300]} ({logp or 'no output log'})", loud=True)

    def raise_alert(self, rec, msg):
        """Write locks/queue/ALERT (the first record; later ones are added under "more") and log loudly."""
        p = self.Q.path("ALERT")
        cur = None
        if os.path.exists(p):
            try:
                cur = H.read_json(p)
            except (OSError, ValueError):
                cur = None
        if isinstance(cur, dict):
            cur.setdefault("more", []).append(rec)
            H.write_json(p, cur)
        else:
            H.write_json(p, rec)
        self.Q.log("ALERT: " + msg + (". Nothing more is submitted until `nrpic-queue clear-alert` (locks/queue/ALERT)"
                                      if rec.get("halts", True) else
                                      ". This record does not halt the dispatcher: it submits nothing while the "
                                      f"count is at or above {H.QUEUE_CAP} (locks/queue/ALERT)"), loud=True)

    def alert(self, e, before, after, fresh, succ, printed):
        rec = {"ts": H.utcnow(), "kind": "rise", "entry": e["id"], "owner": e["owner"], "label": e["label"],
               "command": describe(e), "count_before": len(before), "count_after": len(after),
               "new_jobs": [dict(j, printed_by_the_command=printed_by(j["id"], printed)) for j in fresh],
               "chain_successors": succ,
               "what_to_do": "one route (decision 0033): every card job goes through the dispatcher, so a rise of "
                             "more than one around a dispatch that is not a chain's next segment is a violation. "
                             "Look at squeue, cancel what should not run (scancel <id>), find where each new job "
                             "came from (printed_by_the_command), fix or remove the entry, then: "
                             f"{STOP_LINE.replace(' stop', ' clear-alert')}"}
        self.raise_alert(rec, f"the account's jobs rose by {len(fresh)} (more than one) around {e['id']} "
                              f"{e['owner']}/{e['label']}: {len(before)} before, {len(after)} after; new: "
                              f"{', '.join(j['id'] + ' ' + j['name'] for j in fresh)}")

    # -- the cap keeper (decision 0033): the enforcement that does not depend on the route
    def keep(self):
        """Count the account's jobs (every task of an array one each). An excess above QUEUE_CAP that lasted
        --keeper-confirm seconds (counted again in between; a chain's hand-over lasts seconds) is reported
        (report); nothing is cancelled. The end of an excess is logged; the next one is a new record."""
        self.last_keep = time.time()
        jobs = H.queue_jobs(self.env)
        if jobs is None:
            return
        n = len(jobs)
        if n <= H.QUEUE_CAP:
            if self.in_excess:
                self.Q.log(f"cap keeper: back at {n} of {H.QUEUE_CAP} jobs queued; the excess is over")
            self.in_excess, self.over_since, self.last_reported = False, None, None
            return
        now = time.time()
        if not self.in_excess:
            self.in_excess = True
            self.Q.log(f"cap keeper: {n} jobs of the account queued, above the cap of {H.QUEUE_CAP}; reported if this "
                       f"lasts {self.keeper_confirm:g} s (nothing is cancelled)", loud=True)
        if self.over_since is None:
            self.over_since = now
            return
        if now - self.over_since >= self.keeper_confirm:
            self.report(jobs)
            self.over_since = None               # a changed set must last --keeper-confirm again

    def report(self, jobs):
        """The cap keeper reports an excess; it never cancels a job (decisions on the second review: an
        automatic cancel could hit a job that is not the program's, or cost the program its own runs; the
        dispatcher is the only submitter and holds while the count is at or above the cap, so an excess decays
        by itself, and removing it by hand is the orchestrator's). One ALERT record per distinct set of job ids:
        the count, the entries' jobs, ours without an entry (a run-id name or a working directory under the
        repository: a route past the queue), the user's own, and what to do. The record does not halt
        dispatching: the count rule already holds it, and nothing must stay stopped after the excess has gone."""
        n, excess = len(jobs), len(jobs) - H.QUEUE_CAP
        ids = frozenset(j["id"] for j in jobs)
        if ids == self.last_reported:
            return                               # the same excess as last time: already recorded
        self.last_reported = ids
        cls = classify_jobs(jobs, self.Q.entries(), self.Q.home)
        ent = [dict(j, entry=d) for j, k, d in cls if k == "entry"]
        ours = [dict(j, why=d) for j, k, d in cls if k == "ours"]
        user = [dict(j) for j, k, d in cls if k == "user"]

        def names(js):
            return ", ".join(f"{j['id']} {j['name'] or '-'} {j['state']}" for j in sorted(js, key=jobkey))
        rec = {"ts": H.utcnow(), "kind": "excess", "count": n, "cap": H.QUEUE_CAP, "excess": excess,
               "entries_jobs": ent, "ours_without_entry": ours, "users_own": user, "halts": False,
               "what_to_do": "look (nrpic-queue status, squeue); a job of ours without an entry came by a route past "
                             "the queue: find it and scancel by hand what should not be there; then clear-alert. "
                             f"The dispatcher submits nothing while the count is at or above {H.QUEUE_CAP}, so the "
                             "excess decays by itself; this record does not halt it; the keeper cancels nothing"}
        self.raise_alert(rec, f"cap keeper: {n} jobs of the account queued for {self.keeper_confirm:g} s or more, "
                              f"{excess} above the cap: {len(ent)} of entries, {len(ours)} of ours without an entry"
                              + (f" ({names(ours)})" if ours else "") + f", {len(user)} of the user's own"
                              + (f" ({names(user)})" if user else "") + "; nothing is cancelled")


# ------------------------------------------------------------------ commands

def need_orch(wt, what):
    if wt.owner != "orch" or not wt.is_main:
        raise H.HarnessError(f"`{what}` is the orchestrator's: run it standing in the main checkout ({wt.home})")


def is_orch(cw):
    """The caller stands in the main checkout (the orchestrator)."""
    return cw is not None and cw.is_main and cw.owner == "orch"


def state_worktree(c_opt, sub):
    """Identity from the path (decisions on the review of 2026-11-24): a command that changes state acts on
    the worktree the caller stands in. -C must name that same worktree, except for the orchestrator standing in
    the main checkout, who may name any; the orchestrator's own commands need the caller in the main checkout."""
    home = tool_home()
    cw = cwd_worktree(home)
    if cw is None:
        raise H.HarnessError(f"`{sub}` changes the queue: run it standing in your worktree (the current directory is "
                             f"not inside a worktree of {home}, or lies in a data root of the main checkout)")
    if sub in ORCH_ONLY and not is_orch(cw):
        raise H.HarnessError(f"`{sub}` is the orchestrator's: run it standing in the main checkout ({home})")
    if not c_opt:
        return cw
    tw = resolve_worktree(c_opt, home)
    if tw is None:
        raise H.HarnessError(f"-C {c_opt}: not a worktree of {home} (or it lies in a data root of the main checkout)")
    if tw.root != cw.root and not is_orch(cw):
        raise H.HarnessError(f"-C {c_opt} names {tw.root}, but you stand in {cw.root}: a command that changes the "
                             "queue acts on the worktree you stand in (only the orchestrator, standing in the main "
                             "checkout, names another one)")
    return tw


def may_change(wt, e):
    who = wt.require_owner()
    if who != e["owner"] and who != "orch":
        raise H.HarnessError(f"{e['id']} belongs to {e['owner']}: an owner changes only its own entries (the "
                             "orchestrator any)")
    return who


def normalize_submit(rest):
    a = list(rest)
    if a and os.path.basename(a[0]) == "nrpic-run":
        a = a[1:]
    if a and a[0] == "submit":
        a = a[1:]
    if not a or not a[0].startswith("--"):
        raise H.HarnessError("after -- give the arguments of `nrpic-run submit` (options first, e.g. "
                             "-- --kind scouting --gate G2 --purpose '...' --launcher chain --gpu-hours 4 -- deck.athinput)")
    opts = a[:a.index("--")] if "--" in a else a
    launcher = "local"
    for i, x in enumerate(opts):
        if x == "--launcher" and i + 1 < len(opts):
            launcher = opts[i + 1]
        elif x.startswith("--launcher="):
            launcher = x.split("=", 1)[1]
        elif x in ("--dry-run", "--background", "--wait") or x.startswith("--wait="):
            raise H.HarnessError(f"{x}: not for a queued submission")
    if launcher not in ("batch", "chain"):
        raise H.HarnessError(f"the queue is for card runs (nrpic-run submit --launcher batch|chain); launcher "
                             f"{launcher!r}: run it with nrpic-run directly")
    return a


def dry_run(wt, argv):
    k = argv.index("--") if "--" in argv else len(argv)
    cmd = [sys.executable, "-I", os.path.join(wt.root, "harness", "bin", "nrpic-run"), "submit"] + \
        argv[:k] + ["--dry-run"] + argv[k:]
    r = subprocess.run(cmd, cwd=wt.root, env=H.build_env(wt), capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=900)
    if r.returncode != 0:
        raise H.HarnessError("`nrpic-run submit --dry-run` refused these arguments, so nothing was queued:\n"
                             + tail(r.stderr or r.stdout, 2000) + "\n(--no-check queues them unchecked)")


def cmd_add(wt, args):
    owner = wt.require_owner()
    rest = None
    if "--" in args:
        k = args.index("--")
        args, rest = args[:k], args[k + 1:]
    o = {"label": None, "after": None, "priority": "5", "note": "", "cmd": None}
    check = True
    i = 0
    while i < len(args):
        a = args[i]
        if a == "--no-check":
            check = False
            i += 1
            continue
        key, val = (a.split("=", 1) + [None])[:2] if a.startswith("--") and "=" in a else (a, None)
        if key in ("--label", "--after", "--priority", "--note", "--cmd"):
            if val is None:
                if i + 1 >= len(args):
                    raise H.HarnessError(f"{key} needs a value")
                val = args[i + 1]
                i += 1
            o[key[2:]] = val
            i += 1
            continue
        raise H.HarnessError(f"unknown option {a!r} of add (the arguments of nrpic-run submit go after --)")
    label = o["label"]
    if not label or not LABEL_RX.fullmatch(label):
        raise H.HarnessError("--label L is required: 1 to 48 of [A-Za-z0-9._-]")
    try:
        prio = int(o["priority"])
    except ValueError:
        prio = -1
    if prio < 0:
        raise H.HarnessError("--priority N: an integer, 0 first (default 5)")
    cw = cwd_worktree(wt.home)
    if prio < 2 and not is_orch(cw):
        raise H.HarnessError(f"--priority {prio}: priorities 0 and 1 are given only by the orchestrator, standing in "
                             "the main checkout (0 for runs a user request waits for); ask for it in your outbox. "
                             f"A waiting entry's priority improves by itself by one class per {AGING_HOURS} hours "
                             "(never past 1)")
    if (o["cmd"] is None) == (not rest):
        raise H.HarnessError("give either `-- <arguments of nrpic-run submit>` or `--cmd 'LINE'`, one of the two")
    if rest:
        argv = normalize_submit(rest)
        if check:
            dry_run(wt, argv)
        kind, cmd = "submit", None
    else:
        cmd, argv, kind = o["cmd"], None, "cmd"
        if not cmd.strip():
            raise H.HarnessError("--cmd: empty command line")
        r = subprocess.run(["/bin/bash", "-n", "-c", cmd], capture_output=True, text=True, env=H.boot_env())
        if r.returncode != 0:
            raise H.HarnessError(f"--cmd: bash does not parse it: {r.stderr.strip()}")
    by = cw.owner if cw is not None and cw.owner else None
    Q = Queue(wt.home)
    with Q.lock():
        ents = Q.entries()
        if any(e["owner"] == owner and e["label"] == label and e["state"] in OPEN_STATES for e in ents):
            raise H.HarnessError(f"{owner} already has an entry labelled {label!r} that is not done or removed")
        after_id = None
        if o["after"]:
            c = [e for e in ents if e["owner"] == owner and e["label"] == o["after"] and e["state"] != "removed"]
            if not c:
                raise H.HarnessError(f"--after {o['after']}: no entry of {owner} with that label")
            after_id = c[-1]["id"]
        eid, seq = Q.new_id()
        e = {"schema": SCHEMA, "id": eid, "seq": seq, "owner": owner, "worktree": wt.root, "branch": wt.branch,
             "label": label, "kind": kind, "argv": argv, "cmd": cmd, "after": o["after"], "after_id": after_id,
             "priority": prio, "note": o["note"], "state": "waiting", "added": H.utcnow(),
             "added_by": by or owner, "attempts": 0, "checked": bool(kind == "submit" and check)}
        event(e, f"added by {by or owner}")
        Q.save(e)
        Q.log(f"added {eid} {owner}/{label} p{prio}" + (f" after {o['after']} ({after_id})" if after_id else "")
              + f": {describe(e)[:300]}")
    d = Q.dispatcher()
    print(f"{eid} added: {owner}/{label}, priority {prio}" + (f", after {o['after']} ({after_id})" if after_id else "")
          + ("" if d["alive"] else "; NOTE: no dispatcher is running (nrpic-queue status)"))
    return 0


def cmd_remove(wt, args):
    if len(args) != 1:
        raise H.HarnessError("usage: nrpic-queue remove ID")
    Q = Queue(wt.home)
    e = Q.load(args[0])
    who = may_change(wt, e)

    def upd(x):
        if x["state"] != "waiting":
            raise H.HarnessError(f"{x['id']} is {x['state']}: only a waiting entry is removed")
        x["state"] = "removed"
        event(x, f"removed by {who}")
        return True
    Q.change(e["id"], upd)
    Q.log(f"removed {e['id']} {e['owner']}/{e['label']} by {who}")
    print(f"removed {e['id']} ({e['owner']}/{e['label']})")
    return 0


def cmd_retry(wt, args):
    if len(args) != 1:
        raise H.HarnessError("usage: nrpic-queue retry ID")
    Q = Queue(wt.home)
    e = Q.load(args[0])
    who = may_change(wt, e)
    if e["state"] == "failed" and (e.get("job_name") or e.get("job_ids")):
        jobs = H.queue_jobs(H.build_env(wt))
        if jobs is None:
            raise H.HarnessError("squeue did not answer: cannot tell whether a job of the entry is still queued")
        if job_live(e, jobs):
            raise H.HarnessError(f"{e['id']} submitted job(s) before it failed and one is still in squeue (name "
                                 f"{e.get('job_name')}, ids {e.get('job_ids')}): a retry would submit it again. "
                                 "Wait until it has ended (then `retry`, or `mark-done` if it did what it should), "
                                 "or cancel it (scancel <id>) first")

    def upd(x):
        if x["state"] != "failed":
            raise H.HarnessError(f"{x['id']} is {x['state']}: only a failed entry is retried")
        for k in ("run_id", "job_ids", "job_name"):
            x.pop(k, None)
        x["state"] = "waiting"
        x["last_error"] = x.pop("error", None)
        event(x, f"back to waiting by {who} (retry)")
        return True
    Q.change(e["id"], upd)
    Q.log(f"retry {e['id']} {e['owner']}/{e['label']} by {who}")
    print(f"{e['id']} ({e['owner']}/{e['label']}) is waiting again")
    return 0


def cmd_mark_done(wt, args):
    if len(args) != 1:
        raise H.HarnessError("usage: nrpic-queue mark-done ID")
    Q = Queue(wt.home)
    e = Q.load(args[0])
    who = may_change(wt, e)
    if e["state"] not in ("submitted", "failed"):
        raise H.HarnessError(f"{e['id']} is {e['state']}: only a submitted or failed entry is marked done")
    jobs = H.queue_jobs(H.build_env(wt))
    if jobs is None:
        raise H.HarnessError("squeue did not answer: cannot tell whether a job of the entry is queued")
    if job_live(e, jobs):
        raise H.HarnessError(f"a job of {e['id']} is still in squeue (name {e.get('job_name')}, ids {e.get('job_ids')})")

    def upd(x):
        if x["state"] not in ("submitted", "failed"):
            return False
        x["state"] = "done"
        x["ended"] = H.utcnow()
        event(x, f"marked done by {who} (no job of it in squeue)")
        return True
    Q.change(e["id"], upd)
    Q.log(f"mark-done {e['id']} {e['owner']}/{e['label']} by {who}")
    print(f"{e['id']} ({e['owner']}/{e['label']}) is done")
    return 0


def runjob(e):
    if e.get("run_id"):
        return e["run_id"] + (f" (job {e['job_ids'][0]})" if e.get("job_ids") else "")
    if e.get("job_ids"):
        return "job " + ", ".join(e["job_ids"]) + (f" ({e['job_name']})" if e.get("job_name") else "")
    return "-"


def note_of(e, by_id):
    """The last column of `list`: run and job; why a waiting entry waits; the first line of a failure."""
    if e["state"] == "waiting":
        b = blocked_reason(e, by_id)
        return ("waits: " + b) if b else (wait_text(e) or "-")
    if e["state"] == "failed":
        return "failed: " + (e.get("error_line") or first_line(e.get("error")) or "?")[:160]
    return runjob(e)


def cmd_list(wt, args):
    show_all = "--all" in args
    only = None
    if "--owner" in args:
        k = args.index("--owner")
        only = H.owner_from_short(args[k + 1]) if k + 1 < len(args) else None
        if only is None:
            raise H.HarnessError("--owner ID: an owner id (A, A-emd-pbh, core, kb, orch, ...)")
    Q = Queue(wt.home)
    ents = Q.entries()
    by_id = {e["id"]: e for e in ents}
    now = time.time()
    rows = []
    for e in ents:
        if only and e["owner"] != only:
            continue
        if not show_all and e["state"] in ("done", "removed") and now - (epoch(e.get("updated")) or 0) > 86400:
            continue
        st = e["state"] + ("*" if e["state"] == "waiting" and blocked_reason(e, by_id) else "")
        ep = eff_priority(e, now) if e["state"] == "waiting" else e["priority"]
        pr = str(ep) if ep == e["priority"] else f"{ep}({e['priority']})"
        rows.append(f"{e['id']:6s} {e['owner']:11s} {e['label'][:24]:24s} {st:10s} {pr:>5s} "
                    f"{(e.get('after') or '-')[:16]:16s} {age(e.get('added'), now):>7s}  {note_of(e, by_id)}")
    print(f"{'id':6s} {'owner':11s} {'label':24s} {'state':10s} {'prio':>5s} {'after':16s} {'age':>7s}  "
          "run / job, or why it waits or failed")
    for r in rows:
        print(r)
    print(f"(* waits for its --after entry; prio: the effective priority, the given one in brackets when waiting "
          f"improved it (one class per {AGING_HOURS} h, never past 1)"
          + ("; done and removed entries of the last 24 h shown, --all for every one)" if not show_all else ")"))
    for fn, why in Q.bad:
        print(f"UNREADABLE {os.path.join(Q.edir, fn)}: {why}", file=sys.stderr)
    return 0


def cmd_show(wt, args):
    if len(args) != 1:
        raise H.HarnessError("usage: nrpic-queue show ID")
    Q = Queue(wt.home)
    e = Q.load(args[0])
    print(json.dumps(e, indent=2))
    if e.get("state") == "waiting":
        why = blocked_reason(e, {x["id"]: x for x in Q.entries()})
        w = e.get("wait") or {}
        if why:
            print(f"\nwaits: {why}")
        elif w.get("what"):
            print(f"\n{wait_text(e)}" + (f"; last tried {w['last_try']}" if w.get("last_try") else "")
                  + (f"\n{w['detail']}" if w.get("detail") else ""))
        else:
            print("\nwaits: for a free place in the queue (nrpic-queue status)")
    if e.get("state") == "failed":
        print(f"\nfailed: {e.get('error_line') or first_line(e.get('error'))}   (fix, commit, then: "
              f"harness/bin/nrpic-queue retry {e['id']})")
    if e.get("run_id"):
        print(f"\nquery: harness/bin/nrpic-run status {e['run_id']}   close when its jobs have ended: "
              f"harness/bin/nrpic-run finish {e['run_id']}   (in {e['worktree']})")
    lg = e.get("output_log")
    if lg and os.path.isfile(lg):
        lines = open(lg, errors="replace").read().splitlines()
        print(f"\noutput of the last dispatch ({lg}, last 30 lines):")
        print("\n".join(lines[-30:]))
    return 0


def cmd_status(wt, args):
    Q = Queue(wt.home)
    env = H.build_env(wt)
    jobs = H.queue_jobs(env)
    ents = Q.entries()
    by_id_e = {e["id"]: e for e in ents}
    if jobs is None:
        print("Slurm queue: squeue did not answer")
    else:
        cls = classify_jobs(jobs, ents, wt.home)
        user = [j for j, k, d in cls if k == "user"]
        print(f"Slurm queue: {len(jobs)} of {H.QUEUE_CAP} jobs of the account (decision 0033): {len(jobs) - len(user)} "
              f"of this program, {len(user)} of the user's own")
        for j, k, d in cls:
            if k == "user":
                continue
            e = by_id_e.get(d) if k == "entry" else None
            print(f"  {j['id']:>8s} {j['state']:11s} {j['name'][:40]:40s} "
                  + (f"{e['id']} {e['owner']}/{e['label']}" if e else f"(ours, NOT from the queue: {d})"))
        if user:
            print("  not ours: " + "; ".join(f"{j['id']} {j['name'] or '-'} {j['state']} ({j['workdir'] or 'no workdir'})"
                                         for j in user) + " (the user's own: counted toward the cap)")
        if len(jobs) > H.QUEUE_CAP:
            ours = [j for j, k, d in cls if k == "ours"]
            print(f"EXCESS: {len(jobs)} jobs queued, {len(jobs) - H.QUEUE_CAP} above the cap ({len(jobs) - len(user) - len(ours)} "
                  f"of entries, {len(ours)} of ours without an entry, {len(user)} of the user's own). The dispatcher "
                  "submits nothing until the count is below the cap; nothing is cancelled automatically: look, and "
                  "scancel by hand what should not be there")
    d = Q.dispatcher()
    if d["alive"]:
        poll = float(d.get("poll") or POLL)
        beat = epoch(d.get("beat") or d.get("last_look"))
        old = time.time() - beat if beat else None
        hung = old is None or old > HUNG_LOOKS * poll
        print(f"dispatcher: {'HUNG' if hung else 'running'}, pid {d['pid']}, since {d.get('started')}, heartbeat "
              f"{f'{old:.0f} s' if old is not None else 'never'} ago"
              + (f" (more than {HUNG_LOOKS} looks of {poll:g} s: look at locks/queue/queue.log and nohup.out; "
                 f"stop it ({STOP_LINE}) or end it by its pid)" if hung else
                 f", last look {age(d.get('last_look'))} ago, a look every {poll:g} s, the cap keeper every "
                 f"{float(d.get('keeper') or KEEPER):g} s"))
    else:
        print(f"dispatcher: NOT running (last state {d.get('state', 'never started')}, last heartbeat "
              f"{d.get('beat') or d.get('last_look') or '-'}). Start (orchestrator): {START_LINE}")
    if os.path.exists(Q.path("ALERT")):
        try:
            a = H.read_json(Q.path("ALERT"))
            for r in [a] + list(a.get("more") or []):
                if r.get("kind") == "excess":
                    what = (f"excess: {r.get('count')} jobs queued, {r.get('excess')} above the cap "
                            f"({len(r.get('entries_jobs') or [])} of entries, {len(r.get('ours_without_entry') or [])} "
                            f"of ours without an entry, {len(r.get('users_own') or [])} of the user's own); nothing "
                            "cancelled; does not halt the dispatcher")
                elif r.get("kind") == "cap-keeper":              # records of earlier versions, which cancelled
                    what = (f"cap keeper: {r.get('count')} jobs queued ({r.get('ours', '?')} ours, "
                            f"{r.get('foreign', '?')} the user's own), {r.get('excess')} above the cap; cancelled "
                            f"{', '.join(j['id'] for j in r.get('cancelled') or []) or 'none'}"
                            + (f"; {r['left_above_the_cap']} left above the cap" if r.get("left_above_the_cap") else "")
                            + ("" if r.get("halts", True) else "; does not halt the dispatcher"))
                elif r.get("kind") == "leftover-command":
                    what = f"the command of {r.get('entry')} could not be ended: {r.get('what')}"
                else:
                    what = (f"{r.get('count_before')} -> {r.get('count_after')} jobs around {r.get('entry')} "
                            f"{r.get('owner')}/{r.get('label')}")
                print(f"ALERT since {r.get('ts')}: {what}")
            print(f"  nothing is submitted until clear-alert ({Q.path('ALERT')})" if alert_halts(Q.path("ALERT")) else
                  f"  this ALERT does not halt the dispatcher (the cap keeper's report of an excess); it submits "
                  f"nothing while the count is at or above {H.QUEUE_CAP}; clear it when read ({Q.path('ALERT')})")
        except (OSError, ValueError, AttributeError, TypeError):
            print(f"ALERT: {Q.path('ALERT')} exists; nothing is submitted until clear-alert")
    if os.path.exists(Q.path("STOP")):
        print(f"STOP: {Q.path('STOP')} exists (the dispatcher ends at its next look)")
    counts = {}
    for e in ents:
        counts[e["state"]] = counts.get(e["state"], 0) + 1
    by_id = {e["id"]: e for e in ents}
    blocked = [e for e in ents if e["state"] == "waiting" and blocked_reason(e, by_id)]
    print("entries: " + (", ".join(f"{n} {s}" for s, n in sorted(counts.items())) or "none")
          + (f" ({len(blocked)} of the waiting ones blocked by --after)" if blocked else ""))
    order = dispatch_order(ents)
    if order:
        print("next, in order:")
        for k, e in enumerate(order[:12], 1):
            ep = eff_priority(e)
            print(f"  {k:2d}. {e['id']} {e['owner']:11s} {e['label'][:30]:30s} p{ep}"
                  + (f" (given {e['priority']})" if ep != e["priority"] else "")
                  + (f"  ({wait_text(e)})" if e.get("wait") else ""))
        if len(order) > 12:
            print(f"  ... and {len(order) - 12} more")
    for e in blocked:
        print(f"  blocked: {e['id']} {e['owner']}/{e['label']}: {blocked_reason(e, by_id)}")
    for e in ents:
        if e["state"] == "failed":
            print(f"  failed: {e['id']} {e['owner']}/{e['label']}: "
                  f"{(e.get('error_line') or first_line(e.get('error')))[:160]}")
    return 0


def cmd_run(wt, args):
    need_orch(wt, "run")
    v = {"--poll": POLL, "--cmd-timeout": CMD_TIMEOUT, "--keeper": KEEPER, "--keeper-confirm": KEEPER_CONFIRM}
    i = 0
    while i < len(args):
        if args[i] in v and i + 1 < len(args):
            try:
                x = float(args[i + 1])
            except ValueError:
                x = -1.0
            if x <= 0:
                raise H.HarnessError(f"{args[i]} must be a positive number of seconds")
            v[args[i]] = x
            i += 2
            continue
        raise H.HarnessError(f"unknown option {args[i]!r} of run (--poll S, --cmd-timeout S, --keeper S, "
                             "--keeper-confirm S)")
    return Dispatcher(wt, v["--poll"], v["--cmd-timeout"], v["--keeper"], v["--keeper-confirm"]).run()


def cmd_check_dispatch(wt, args):
    """Exit 0 only when the marker in this process's environment is valid now: the entry it names is being
    dispatched with that token, belongs to this worktree's owner and worktree, and the dispatcher holds the
    submit lock. A wrapper given with --cmd calls this, never `[ -n "$NRPIC_QUEUE_DISPATCH" ]`: the variable
    is inherited by every job the wrapper submits itself, and stays set there after the dispatch."""
    why = H.queue_dispatch_problem(wt)
    if why is None:
        print(f"valid: {os.environ.get(H.QUEUE_DISPATCH_VAR, '').split(':', 1)[0]} is being dispatched in {wt.root}")
        return 0
    print(f"not inside a dispatch: {why}", file=sys.stderr)
    return 1


def cmd_stop(wt, args):
    need_orch(wt, "stop")
    try:
        wait = float(args[args.index("--wait") + 1]) if "--wait" in args else 60.0
    except (IndexError, ValueError):
        raise H.HarnessError("usage: nrpic-queue stop [--wait SECONDS]")
    Q = Queue(wt.home).ensure()
    d = Q.dispatcher()
    if not d["alive"]:
        print("no dispatcher is running; nothing to stop")
        return 0
    with open(Q.path("STOP"), "w") as f:
        f.write(f"stop asked {H.utcnow()}\n")
    Q.log(f"STOP written (dispatcher pid {d['pid']})")
    t_end = time.time() + wait
    while time.time() < t_end and pid_alive(d["pid"]):
        time.sleep(0.5)
    if pid_alive(d["pid"]):
        print(f"STOP written; the dispatcher (pid {d['pid']}) has not ended within {wait:g} s (an entry's command "
              "may be running); it ends after it")
        return 1
    print(f"the dispatcher (pid {d['pid']}) has ended; queued card jobs are left as they are")
    return 0


def cmd_clear_alert(wt, args):
    need_orch(wt, "clear-alert")
    Q = Queue(wt.home).ensure()
    p = Q.path("ALERT")
    if not os.path.exists(p):
        print("no ALERT")
        return 0
    dst = Q.path(f"ALERT.cleared-{time.strftime('%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ', time.gmtime())}")
    os.replace(p, dst)
    Q.log(f"ALERT cleared by the orchestrator (kept as {os.path.basename(dst)}): submissions resume")
    print(f"ALERT cleared (kept as {dst}); the dispatcher submits again at its next look")
    return 0


COMMANDS = {"add": (cmd_add, True), "remove": (cmd_remove, True), "retry": (cmd_retry, True),
            "mark-done": (cmd_mark_done, True), "list": (cmd_list, False), "show": (cmd_show, False),
            "status": (cmd_status, False), "run": (cmd_run, True), "stop": (cmd_stop, True),
            "clear-alert": (cmd_clear_alert, True), "check-dispatch": (cmd_check_dispatch, True)}


def main(argv):
    try:
        c_opt, rest = H.strip_options_prefix(argv)
        if not rest or rest[0] in ("-h", "--help", "help"):
            print(__doc__)
            return 0 if rest else 2
        sub, args = rest[0], rest[1:]
        opts = args[:args.index("--")] if "--" in args else args
        if "-h" in opts or "--help" in opts:
            print(__doc__)
            return 0
        if sub not in COMMANDS:
            print(__doc__)
            return 2
        fn, strict = COMMANDS[sub]
        wt = state_worktree(c_opt, sub) if sub in STATE_CHANGING else acting_worktree(c_opt, strict=strict)
        return fn(wt, args) or 0
    except H.HarnessError as e:
        print(f"nrpic-queue: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
